{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1782262503,"nonce":"FloLvYI/2Xd50iqMsBrewC/SbVc=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABGfGAn87H2hXO"},"target":"daef9df9520e99f8302fb6c44f3e7c1c12b0ac1880d262ccdb54027882f1672b","message":"## Correction to the original framing\n\nThe original title/body of this issue (\"no low-battery alarm fired\") was **wrong** — it came from a field-log overstatement. **The annunciator DID fire** (went yellow at the 23.0 V `BATT_LOW_VOLT` threshold ~15:05; #171/#162 fix working as designed); the operator saw it and advised the pilot to return at 2 kt. The thresholds are correctly set (`BATT_LOW_VOLT` 23.0 V, `BATT_CRT_VOLT` 21.5 V) and documented in `bizzyboat_power.md`. The boat still ran out and was towed in — but **not because the alarm failed**.\n\n## Real finding — the turn-back trigger had no distance reserve\n\nBag analysis of the 2026-06-23 full-discharge ([#313](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/313)) shows:\n\n- The boat surveyed a box **~1.5–2 nm from the dock**; it had ample energy margin to return for almost the whole mission.\n- **The annunciator yellow (23.0 V loaded, 15:05:41) and the point of no return (~22.9 V, 15:07:45) were ~2 minutes apart.** At the warning there was only ~10 % margin (+0.17 nm of homeward reach), and only if the boat turned straight home that instant.\n- The boat kept running the survey pattern for ~20 min after the warning instead of beelining home, so it blew through the point of no return and died **1.29 nm short** of the dock.\n\nSo for a boat operating ~1.5–2 nm out, **23 V is already too late** — the ladder's \"23 V ≈ 1 h\" is a *time* figure, not *homeward reach*.\n\n## Proposed fix (refocused)\n\n1. **Distance-aware \"bingo\" reserve rule** — turn back when `track-left-in-tank ≈ 1.3–1.5 × straight-line distance home`, not at a fixed voltage. Interim rule for ops within ~2 nm: treat **~23.5–24 V loaded** as turn-back, and **go straight home on the warning — don't finish the line.**\n2. **Consider enabling `BATT_FS_LOW_ACT`** (auto-RTL/HOLD) for normal survey ops — it's intentionally `0` for drain tests, but today wasn't a drain test.\n3. **Current sensing (#88)** for true SOC / time-remaining, which a fixed voltage threshold can't give.\n\nEvidence: `docs/analysis/2026-06-23/` (departure/charger, distance/speed, turn-back plots + dev log). Part of #313; feeds #167 (this is the first real full-charge-to-cutoff datapoint). Annunciator behaviour cross-refs #171/#162.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":5,"timestamp":1782256406,"nonce":"9we/7F2Hji1j7SUOYfPsjBFP4qU=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABGfGAn88AAAAGUGG63g"},"added":["deployment"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"timestamp":1782256406,"nonce":"6+nv5DAwSzs/KZq0nFkW91soCfk=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABGfGAn88AAAAGUGG7DA"},"added":["rca"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"timestamp":1782257084,"nonce":"7vVoNW5lGTKe6u9lkMHMg6EtxUc=","metadata":{"github-id":"UNLE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABGfGAn88AAAAGUGaFGA"},"added":[],"removed":["deployment"]},{"type":2,"timestamp":1782262503,"nonce":"a7NzO2B6ecYFEZCgwEKd7GrXzyU=","metadata":{"github-id":"RTE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABGfGAn88AAAAGUIh5oA"},"title":"Battery turn-back trigger has no distance reserve → power exhaustion 1.29 nm from dock (2026-06-23 Massabesic)","was":"Battery turn-back trigger has no distance reserve → power exhaustion 1.29 nm from dock (2026-06-23 Massabesic)"},{"type":4,"timestamp":1782266647,"nonce":"kVwk5kv9L9R8eBn50AibViSwVPc=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABGfGAn88AAAAGUKPcGw"},"status":2}]}